{"description":"The CLI could not describe its own command surface to a machine. An agent had to scrape human help text to learn a command's flags and whether they are repeatable, and `eka schema` did not exist (exit 2, unknown command). `eka manifest --json` describes workspace and repository identity, not the command surface.","impact":"Every agent session paid the discovery cost in tokens and in wrong guesses. The information already existed in the cobra command definitions; it was merely not exposed. Fixed by `eka schema [--json]`, which generates the report from the live command tree so it cannot drift from behaviour."}